{"type": "response", "step": 4, "latency_s": 5.617988, "message": {"id": "msg_011Cgm7aHU61QzGhj2DU6xV5", "container": null, "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I couldn't make the change. The lakehouse's policy blocked the update and nothing was modified.\n\n**What happened:** I ran `UPDATE db.customers_pii SET national_id = NULL`, and it was denied for two reasons:\n1. `db.customers_pii` is a protected table, so it can't be modified.\n2. The update had no WHERE clause, so it would have touched every row.\n\nI didn't try to get around this, for example by adding a dummy WHERE clause. That wouldn't fix the protected-table block, and the policy is clearly meant to stop exactly this kind of change.\n\n**Current state:** All 60 rows still have a `national_id` value.\n\n**What you'd need to do:**\n- **Ask the table's owner or the platform admin** to remove the protection or make the change themselves. The compliance requirement you described should support the request.\n- **Plan to clean up old snapshots too.** Setting the column to NULL only changes the current version of the table. The table has two older snapshots (100014 from 2026-07-27 and 100015 from 2026-10-23) that still hold the national IDs, and anyone can read them through time travel. Once the NULL update is in, you'd need to expire those snapshots and then remove orphan files to actually delete the data. Snapshot expiry can't be undone, so I'd only do it with explicit sign-off.\n\nOnce the table can be changed, I can run the update and the cleanup.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1680, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 864, "output_tokens": 456, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "s